# Matreshka Remap — what git does not carry.
#
# The rule: source and the baked .npz tables are tracked. Anything a build
# step, a Blender bake, an export script or a render run can put back is not.


# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/


# --- Build output -----------------------------------------------------------
# tool/build is PyInstaller's work directory (93 MB), tool/dist its result.
build/
dist/
*.spec.bak

# Shipped binaries and the archives they are packed into. Rebuilt by
# build.bat / build_mac.sh / pack_mac.py.
*.exe
*.zip
*.rar
*.7z


# --- mac_build --------------------------------------------------------------
# pack_mac.py copies the app sources, requirements.txt and tables/*.npz here
# from tool/ and converts line endings. Those copies are generated — the
# originals in tool/ are what is tracked.
#
# The Mac-only files that live here and nowhere else (README_MAC.md,
# build_mac.sh, build.spec, entitlements.plist, README.md) stay tracked.
/mac_build/*.py
/mac_build/requirements.txt
/mac_build/tables/
/mac_build/Check.png


# --- Baked tables -----------------------------------------------------------
# The .npz ARE tracked: they are what the renderer reads, and remaking them
# needs Blender plus the .blend scene. They total about 5.5 MB.
#
# The EXRs are not, and there are three sets of them (~29 MB in all):
#   tool/tables/*.exr        the sharp reference pass from bake_tables.py
#   tool/tables/st/*.exr     written from the npz by export_tables_exr.py
#   fusion_plugin/Macros/    byte-identical copies of tables/st, installed
#                            into Resolve by copy_to_resolve.py
*.exr


# --- Media, renders, working state ------------------------------------------
# Sources and results. 3.6 GB between them; none of it is source code.
/ToRemap/
/OUT/
/Remaped/
/Snapshots/
/Flipbook/
/Logs/
*.mp4
*.mov
*.mxf
*.prores

# Blender autosave. The scene itself (zaryadye_remap_v1.blend) is tracked.
*.blend1
*.blend2

# Written by the application while it runs, not a setting anyone edits.
# tool/remap_tool.json -- the shipped default, three lines of it -- stays
# tracked. The one beside the .blend holds the framing aimed on every clip,
# which is work, and so are the rolling backups beside it.
/remap_tool.json*
/remap_presets.json*
/ui_span.txt
*.log


# --- Generated beside the source --------------------------------------------
# pack_mac.py copies tool/icons here the same way it copies the tables.
/mac_build/icons/

# The checks write their fixtures here -- a short sequence, a few stills, and
# the copy of remap_tool.json they put back afterwards.
/tool/tests/_scratch/

# A Blender render, 25 MB of it. Output, like everything in OUT.
/Blender_OUT_Render.png


# --- Stray -------------------------------------------------------------------
.__perm_test


# --- OS / editors -----------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
